@demandrecords @grichadev I don’t code for human readability anymore.
As long as the agents find simple ways and don’t pile bugs it’s good. I’m often guiding smaller models on architecture, SOC etc…
If you ask simple things and the agents create bugs or take too much time I read logs and ask to refactor

@forgebitz What’s important is building a system of review that is not 100% code focus.
Sometimes I read the code, sometimes only the slowed E2E videos.
what’s important is that there is a loop at the end of the impl for the agent where he can check against and retry if it’s not good enough

@forgebitz For me it’s not about “writing tests” it’s about testing what just have been implemented.
It could be unit testing, could be E2E testing, could be just screen capture
Could be all of this with other AI behind it to review and score them and loop until good etc…

